🔹 But What Are We Studying?

Since LLMs already know everything they will ever know before deployment, we are studying what happens before that stage:

We are investigating:

✅ What structures form during training?
	•	How do embeddings go from random noise to meaningful representations?
	•	Do we see geometric structures like manifolds or spirals emerge in embedding space?

✅ How does self-attention evolve?
	•	Does attention start random and then sharpen into focused token relationships?
	•	Do certain words always become “key tokens” during learning?

✅ How does the transformer compress information?
	•	Do we see singular value collapse in FFNs as redundant information is removed?
	•	Does the network become more efficient over time?

✅ What mathematical principles govern training?
	•	Does transformer training follow power laws, symmetry, or phase transitions?
	•	Can we predict when learning will accelerate based on entropy reduction?